  "body": "Per #28, it seems the whole purpose of .replace() is to put the new token in the same place as the old one.  The implementation in Gecko doesn't actually do that.  The current spec says just \"Replace token in tokens with newToken\", which is not absolutely explicit that order should be preserved.  I think this could use clarification, since the term \"replace\" is not formally defined anywhere.\n",
